    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d494-a8">

                <pb facs="0552" n="502" xml:id="pg502"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 8 in No. 122.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Tyler to the Sadr Azem.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Teheran</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1894-08-21"><hi rendition="#italic">August 21,
                        1894</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Your Highness</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge
                    the receipt of your letter of the 18th of Safar, A. H. 1312 (corresponding to
                    the 20th of August), informing me that stringent orders had been sent to the
                    authorities of Hamadan to preserve the peace of the town and to afford all
                    protection to the lives and property of American citizens.</p>
                <p>I beg to tender on the part of the U. S. Government and the missionaries their
                    sincere thanks for this action of your highness, which I trust will have the
                    effect of curbing the turbulent elements and of permitting the missionaries to
                    carry on their work of charity in the future, free from anxiety and
                    annoyance.</p>
                <p>I take this opportunity, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Tyler.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
